ng a daily record. Since 2000, Lander has set <strong class=\"sig\">32 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 72 that chance alone would give, and <strong class=\"sig\">164 record highs</strong>, far more than the 72 that chance alone would give. The 2020s hold the most record highs of any decade (75). Lander's all-time high is 102\u00b0F, on July 27, 1935.","t_chg":"Lander's days and nights both warmed. Nights warmed faster.","p_chg":"Across 133 complete years: Lander's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.42\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.35 to +0.48), about +5.5\u00b0F since 1892. Lander's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.18\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.10 to +0.26), about +2.4\u00b0F since 1892.","t_mon":"Lows rose in all 12 months. Highs rose in 5 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Lander's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.07 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 13.0 inches a year. The wettest year was 1957 (21.89 in); the driest, 2001 (5.38 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 29 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}